  "prose": {
    "path": "/tmp/zfc-open-schema-templates/independent-review-bic-final.md",
    "sha256": "017758316ee61c15dbf635aeaef209f6a897f6a7dd25c0da3aed3409c3d9a700",
    "text": "# Final OpenSchemaTemplates independent review\n\nCLEAN: complete final source, five-probe/five-caller audit, full guarded checker and exact run3 evidence reviewed without running Lean or rerunning the checker. All64 before/after inputs, actual selected providers and fresh object were independently rehashed. The author run3 is the first complete PASS; run1/run2 failures remain distinct. One unused-simp argument warning in the Separation normalization is retained, with zero audit warnings.\n\nSeparation keeps `z=#0,y=#1,x=#2`, with the matrix substituted at `#0`. Replacement is the globally total functional schema: the functional premise uses matrix slots `[#1,#0]`, its uniqueness comparison uses `[#2,#0]` and native equality `#0=#1`, and the image clause uses `[#0,#1]` with `x in X` at slots0/3. The ordinary source equality and membership symbols remain the literal set-theoretic ones. No arbitrary nonfunctional Collection callback is supplied.\n\nThe two normalization lemmas commute actual native translation with these exact schema skeletons. Primitive/notation negation laws, bound-variable translation and empty finite-vector normalization leave every source statement unchanged. The final `rfl` closes definitional literal relation/vector equalities. The lifted-axiom callback first applies `TProof.byAxm`, then eliminates the external `lMap` existential into the remaining membership proposition. Thus its Type-valued proof uses legal Prop elimination and the same actual quoted ZF membership proof; no selector or stronger axiom hypothesis is added.\n\n`separationProof` and `replacementProof` use checked `closeTemplate` for every external finite buffer and actual checked internal ZF schema proof constructors. They close only the ordinary source free-variable range. Internal predicate matrices may have arbitrary additional internal free parameters, which remain free. Source template syntax, its parameter range and proof carrier construction remain externally finite; there is no claim to arbitrary internal source proof compilation.\n\nThe guard freezes both source/audit and exact Closure/OpenSchemaAxioms evidence, verifies their shared source/object identities, the18-project import closure and seven boundary providers against pinned dependency/compiler metadata, selects actual first providers including Init/Omega, snapshots fresh source/audit, and checks pre/post input/provider/object stability. Only the new source and audit are freshly compiled with4GiB/one thread. No dependency build/download or whole-Foundation-cache attestation is made.\n\nNo numerical proof-search, internal L2, binary-machine, consistency or new state-bound endpoint follows from this callback module alone. This independent review rehashed recorded artifacts and read proofs/guards; it did not perform a proof or checker replay.\n"
  },
  "scope": "Proof, audit, executed guard and final PASS independently read/rehashed without proof/checker replay; author separately prepared publication archive and metadata-only maintained-default check."
}
